// Img:(Blah,Blah.png)   SOFT    SIMPLE    Scale:0.X    Low:0.Y    Pack:name  or   Volatile:name  or   Volpack:name
// SOFT means treat as soft edged, as above.
// SIMPLE means ‘don’t turn into strips’. Handy for images used in particle effects, to keep the polygon count down. NB: images used in ‘tile’ commands are automatically tagged as ‘simple’
// Scale:0.X means ‘scale the source image down to 0.X of its original size before packing into the hi-res assets’ (If you don’t specify ‘Scale:’ then a value of 1.0 is used)
// Low:0.Y means ‘scale the source image down to 0.Y of its original size before packing into the LOW-RES assets’ (if you don’t specify ‘Low:’ then a value of 0.5 x Scale is used)
// Volatile:name means this image (and others with the same tag) should be put into the same Atlas and loaded/unloaded as needed rather than staying in memory all the time. Good for things like the different pitch locales in Cricket, to save on run-time memory.


